From: Elizabeth Schwartz <betsys@cs.umb.edu>
Date: Wed, 7 Dec 1994 09:23:34 -0500 (EST)
Subject: [#94-12-277] META: ways to make reading this list easier

If you are on a Unix box, check out "deliver" or "procmail" or the "pine" 
mail program. All of these have ways to sort mail into different boxes. 
I use deliver, which lets me sort on the "From" "To" "CC" or "Subject"
fields, using regexps. I can kill mail from a given sender without
ever seeing it.

  For Unix mail, I like Elm. Elm can sort the mail folder on the fly, by
date, length, or subject (among other things) and will limit the display
based on sender or subject.

With a high volume list like extropians, I sometimes sort by *size*, since
the biggest posts are often forwards or flames, and the smallest posts are
often errors. I flip through those, then look at the subjects.

  If you are using a PC, look into some of the QWK-based mail readers. I
haven't played with getting net mail into QWK format, but the QWK readers
are very sophisticated.

good luck,
Betsy

