From: "W. Scott Meeks" <meeks@osf.org>
Date: Wed, 07 Dec 1994 13:48:43 -0500
Subject: [#94-12-282] can we change this Mailing List into a NEWSGROUP ?? and why 

With one important exception, I find using the list management tools even
better than a newsgroup.  Here's how I use the list.  First, I exclude
everything and turned on notification of filtered messages.  Then I read
the subjects and resend any messages that look interesting.  If a whole
thread appears that looks interesting, I can resend that and even include
it for the future and exclude it later if it plays out.  So it's very
similar to reading a newsgroup with a threaded newsreader. 

The important exception is that the holding period for messages is
relatively short, variable, and you can't know when a message has expired
without trying to retrieve it.  Ideally, expired messages should go to some
higher density, slower retrieval storage, but I don't know how feasible
that is.

